@meta
id: 26-07
title: Drill — this line, through a command
chapter: 26
type: drill
skills: filter-bang
par: 21
minutes: 5
reps: 8
vscode: select the line, retype it in capitals
open: error-code.txt

@brief
Eight times: put line 2 through `tr a-z A-Z` so the error code is in
upper case. Line 1 is a comment and stays as it is.

@keys
| `!!` | filter this line |
| `tr a-z A-Z` | upper case |

@hints
One `j` to get onto the line, then double the bang.
--
`j` then `!!tr a-z A-Z` and Enter.

@solution
    j  !!tr a-z A-Z<Enter>  :wq<Enter>

`!!` is the filter you will use most often, because most of the time the
thing you want to run a command on is the line you are already looking
at: a base64 blob to decode, a JSON line to pretty-print, a path to
expand, a number to convert. The command changes every time and the two
keys in front of it never do.

@start error-code.txt
# the constant below must match the key in default.json
refund_window_expired

@expected error-code.txt
# the constant below must match the key in default.json
REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED
